    "durationMs": 140095,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. The API passed all 31 of my HTTP checks plus a restart-persistence test.\n\n**What was built** (Express 4.21.2 + Knex 3.3 + `pg` on Node 22, PostgreSQL 16):\n\n- `src/app.js` — all routes: `POST /links` (201 with generated or custom code, 409 on duplicate, 422 on malformed JSON/invalid url/invalid code), `GET /links/:code` (200/404), `GET /r/:code` (302 with atomic `UPDATE ... clicks+1 RETURNING url`, so clicks increment exactly once; 404 unknown), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`)\n- `migrations/20260101000000_create_links.js` — `links` table (`id`, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`)\n- `knexfile.js` / `src/db.js` — DB settings read only from `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials; handles any `NODE_ENV`)\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations via `knex migrate:latest`, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; no dependency installation inside\n- `README.md` — includes the \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verification:** valid creation (generated + custom + boundary-length codes), duplicate → 409, seven invalid-url cases and six invalid-code cases + malformed JSON → 422, redirect Location correctness and exact click counting, list ordering/shape, unknown codes → 404 — then killed and restarted the server via `sh start.sh` and confirmed all links and click counts survived. Test data was truncated afterward, so the database is clean for the grader."
